Storage of flammable liquids in tanks — HSE HSG176 (@cs-hsg176: 0, is #reference, #part-of @cs-sources) { r_3J96NXWJF945DTPAPBRQPT177R
UK Health and Safety Executive. Storage of flammable liquids in tanks, HSG176, second edition, 2015, ISBN 9780717666072. [Official record](https://www.hse.gov.uk/pubns/books/hsg176.htm) · [Complete 69-file-page guide](https://www.hse.gov.uk/pubns/priced/hsg176.pdf).

Read the full guide for its stated tank/storage domain. Study layout, containment, piping, contents measurement, loading/unloading, inspection and operating change together. Its near-atmospheric flammable-liquid scope is distinct from pressure-gas, cryogenic or reactive-substance equipment.

Publication identity, scope and contents were inspected on 29 October 2026. The publisher supplies authorized free access; the site OGL and actual publication/component notices should be kept together. This is a dated technical guide, not a current global tank code or a completed design. External product-specific and local requirements remain part of the reading case. No PDF is copied here.

